  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 14, P = 15. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[8, 1, 10, 12, 1, 7, 2, 3, 10, 5, 11, 3, 12, 8], [2, 2, 14, 14, 13, 12, 12, 10, 9, 13, 14, 3, 8, 6], [5, 3, 8, 1, 11, 7, 8, 14, 9, 12, 5, 11, 13, 13]], sigma = [4, 13, 5, 10, 0, 2, 11, 8, 7, 12, 3, 6, 9, 1], B = [10, 9, 6, 0, 10, 6, 5, 4, 4, 12, 0, 5, 12, 9].",
  "references": [
   "arXiv:2609.30069",
   "https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data"
  ],
  "date": "2026",
  "novelty": "known_parameters",
  "notes": "Literature baseline: a reproduction of a code published with arXiv:2609.30069, rebuilt from the authors' data repository (https://github.com/ultra-high-rate-qec/design-principles-data/blob/306b31d/codes/reverse_fold/j3l14/specs/reverse_j3l14_p15_k62.json). Not a new construction. The authors report d = 4 as exact. Their lower-bound search output is not in the repository, so this entry carries an upper bound backed by their weight-4 Pauli logical, stored as the witness."
